  "body": "### What happened\n\nOn current main (`fc9b297`), the batch gate fails in\n`camcraft-motion --test swarf_pose_continuity`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCARGO_HOME=/tmp/camcraft-cargo cargo test --locked -p camcraft-motion --test swarf_pose_continuity -- --nocapture\n\nThe two-pass advanced swarf path reports:\n- Debug band: 53 air links; test limit is 51.\n- Full band: 86 air links; test limit is 84.\n\nThe counts repeat on a standalone run. The two additional links occur at\ncoarse-pass raster ends. They move pose changes into air; the test reports\nzero cutting turns past the 30-degree guard. The plain swarf counts still\nmeet their limits.\n\nUpdate the link limits if these guarded links are acceptable, while\nretaining the cutting-turn and flank-clearance checks. The targeted test\npasses with limits of 53 and 86.\n\n### camcraft version and OS\n\n0.14+ Linux\n\n### Screenshots or recording\n\n_No response_",
